<.shell current={:person_head}>
  <h1>Person head</h1>
  <p class="lead">A member's photo, name, standing, and facts.</p>

  <div class="demo">
    <.person_head
      id="person-head-demo"
      name="Sam Rivera"
      photo={~p"/images/sam-rivera.jpg"}
      facts={["Ground searcher", "Joined October 2016", "Last attended Sep 30, 2026"]}
    >
      <:actions>
        <.button>View as member</.button>
      </:actions>
    </.person_head>
  </div>

  <div class="demo">
    <.person_head
      id="person-head-away-demo"
      name="Alex Chen"
      photo="/styles/no-photo.png"
      standing={{:away, %{ends_on: ~D[2026-11-30]}}}
      facts={["Joined March 2019", "Last attended Aug 2, 2026"]}
    />
  </div>

  <h3>A team</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <.person_head id="person-head-team-demo" name="Coast Range SAR">
      <:picture>
        <span class="team-head-logo is-initials">CR</span>
      </:picture>
      <:line>
        Refreshed 4 min ago ·
        <.button type="button" variant={:link} size={:sm}>Refresh now</.button>
      </:line>
    </.person_head>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>
    The top of a member's own page: the team member page, on every tab, and Your membership.
    A team's Dashboard opens with it too, its square logo in the photo's place.
  </p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>
    Any other page's title, which is a plain <code>h1</code>. A member in a list or table is a row.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul class="list">
    <li>
      The photo comes in with the refresh. When there is none, the page path answers 404 and the circle shows the member's initials.
    </li>
    <li>
      A badge beside the name when the member isn't active: amber for Away until a date, grey for Retired and Not a person. The reason stays on the Standing tab.
    </li>
    <li>
      One line of facts: role, when they joined, and when they last attended. A fact the team's records don't have is left out. No member ID: teams number members in very different ways.
    </li>
    <li>Buttons sit on the right and wrap under the name on a narrow screen.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.person_head id name photo standing facts&gt;</code>
    with standing from <code>Standing.today/3</code>
    and facts from <code>PersonHead.facts/3</code>. Buttons go in <code>:actions</code>.
    A team's logo goes in <code>:picture</code>, and a line with a button in <code>:line</code>.
  </p>
</.shell>
